{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2599 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "412a1150df09b43f645eff8922652961e03829ecda855b6d85b461647b03d6a5" :edb/db-before-t 2598 :edb/db-after-t 2599 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535911 50 #inst "2026-10-09T10:29:09.288Z" 13194139535911 true] [17592186059508 1100 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." 13194139535911 false] [17592186059508 1100 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/assets/67d01790cfbda1f20a23c9e22a64714156485851ce56b2f73e9873db6ef4bed8.png)\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." 13194139535911 true] [17592186059508 1145 "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2y=0 \\\\ y=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=1$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+2(1)=0 \n\t\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\n\tx=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=1.$ Or, in vector form, $\\left<  -2,1 \\right>.$" 13194139535911 false] [17592186059508 1145 "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/assets/da9c44be043ad3a15808a9e0dd77636697170047e61b73a0d591bc3581d992fb.png)\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=1$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+2(1)=0 \n\t\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\n\tx=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=1.$ Or, in vector form, $\\left<  -2,1 \\right>.$" 13194139535911 true] [17592186059509 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+5y=5 \\\\ x-6y=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139535911 false] [17592186059509 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/assets/a80ecf94bbd4f0ea4b7a860e340039ca80bc5ccd0d2a19503cb9dcc571558976.png)\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139535911 true] [17592186059509 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/assets/ab29f353f00454b6e8eeb490336e2b33d0b2cf6cd47f4d24ac6c8a8f042af628.png)\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071933/assets/ee5b759f55931cf4935a0763f22c9eb5deedb04f3e247c295aa2a1da09b121b4.png)\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-10$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-5(-10)=-5 \n\t\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\n\tx=-55.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-55$ and $y=-10.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -55,-10 \\rangle.$" 13194139535911 true] [17592186059509 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-5y=-5 \\\\ y=-10,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-10$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-5(-10)=-5 \n\t\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\n\tx=-55.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-55$ and $y=-10.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -55,-10 \\rangle.$" 13194139535911 false] [17592186059700 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374032 13194139535911 true] [17592186059700 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374039 13194139535911 true] [17592186059700 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374046 13194139535911 true] [17592186059701 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374053 13194139535911 true] [17592186059701 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374060 13194139535911 true] [17592186059701 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374067 13194139535911 true] [17592186374032 1017 #edb/ref 17592186374033 13194139535911 true] [17592186374032 1089 "q-1060" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374032 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535911 true] [17592186374032 1100 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." 13194139535911 true] [17592186374032 1113 #uuid "b2cfb536-5e1c-504f-8c3c-31308e0bec9d" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374032 1145 "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form using the standard algorithm for Gaussian elimination, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 16 & 13\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{16}\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{13}{16}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374033 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374034 13194139535911 true] [17592186374033 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374035 13194139535911 true] [17592186374033 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374036 13194139535911 true] [17592186374033 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374037 13194139535911 true] [17592186374033 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374038 13194139535911 true] [17592186374033 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535911 true] [17592186374033 1041 "selection" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374033 1104 #edb/ref 17592186374037 13194139535911 true] [17592186374033 1110 #uuid "70639cf9-3345-5368-8a0c-fe1ec47ac05e" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374034 1034 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{11}{16}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374034 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535911 true] [17592186374034 1111 #uuid "f7b8eba7-bf5b-584b-97e8-00c5e40e9ff7" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374035 1034 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{15}{16}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374035 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535911 true] [17592186374035 1111 #uuid "b4c35b62-c01f-5354-8208-d5cec20a0def" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374036 1034 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{17}{16}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374036 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535911 true] [17592186374036 1111 #uuid "a2d647a6-278c-5994-97ee-7870c8878ccd" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374037 1034 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{13}{16}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374037 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535911 true] [17592186374037 1111 #uuid "497a9b0b-c34d-5915-9660-80e41049ff66" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374038 1034 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{9}{16}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374038 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535911 true] [17592186374038 1111 #uuid "fc38113a-0010-59ce-b64d-9837a0b810fa" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374039 1017 #edb/ref 17592186374040 13194139535911 true] [17592186374039 1089 "q-130910" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374039 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535911 true] [17592186374039 1100 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." 13194139535911 true] [17592186374039 1113 #uuid "36655489-58cf-5b95-a28e-946cf05f7596" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374039 1145 "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+7y=-2 \\\\  & y=-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-1$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+7(-1)=-2\\,⇒\\,x=-2+7=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=5$ and $y=-1.$" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374040 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374041 13194139535911 true] [17592186374040 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374042 13194139535911 true] [17592186374040 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374043 13194139535911 true] [17592186374040 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374044 13194139535911 true] [17592186374040 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374045 13194139535911 true] [17592186374040 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535911 true] [17592186374040 1041 "selection" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374040 1104 #edb/ref 17592186374044 13194139535911 true] [17592186374040 1110 #uuid "791e5a06-2eba-5ca0-8882-261a36070737" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374041 1034 "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,x=15$ and $y=1$" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374041 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535911 true] [17592186374041 1111 #uuid "0dc543b6-459a-5fcf-8011-b02a2730bbb9" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374042 1034 "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,x=12$ and $y=-2$" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374042 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535911 true] [17592186374042 1111 #uuid "a07b071b-1df7-545e-9f12-03b5ebe08484" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374043 1034 "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,x=13$ and $y=-1$" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374043 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535911 true] [17592186374043 1111 #uuid "4b49eddc-f0db-5c41-9338-2b3ca8cdf682" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374044 1034 "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,x=5$ and $y=-1$" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374044 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535911 true] [17592186374044 1111 #uuid "783a60bc-1579-5f45-aecf-c05de1a26b75" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374045 1034 "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,x=12$ and $y=2$" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374045 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535911 true] [17592186374045 1111 #uuid "ccf8fb30-5ac9-50da-a4bf-09f50dd3b3c0" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374046 1017 #edb/ref 17592186374047 13194139535911 true] [17592186374046 1089 "q-20461" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374046 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535911 true] [17592186374046 1100 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 & -9 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." 13194139535911 true] [17592186374046 1113 #uuid "0371d28b-41aa-5288-a97c-eeca95bd4c3f" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374046 1145 "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 & -9 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 1 & -2 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-3y=-\\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & y=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=\\frac{1}{2}$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-3(\\frac{1}{2})=-\\frac{9}{2}\\,⇒\\,x=-\\frac{9}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}=-3.\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-3$ and $y=\\frac{1}{2}.$" 13194139535911 true] [17592186374047 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374048 13194139535911 true] [17592186374047 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374049 13194139535911 true] [17592186374047 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374050 13194139535911 true] [17592186374047 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374051 13194139535911 true] [17592186374047 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374052 13194139535911 true